OK, so I found the answer ;)
Initially I found a program that would do this, then I found the source code to xset.c After looking through that I realised that you *can* set the repeat mode for an individual key using xset, the syntax is

# turn repeat on for keycode
 xset r <keycode>

# turn repeat off for keycode
 xset -r <keycode>

Blimey, I've used xset for a lot of years, I guess there is always some option in Unix that you don't find till you need it ;)

To run after login to an Xserver I created a .X11Startup file:

xmodmap .dxkeycaps
xset r 92
xset r 97

Now my Alt_L and Alt_R don't auto-repeat.

Regards, Mark. 


